#!/usr/bin/env python3
# ==== Copyright Valve Corporation, All rights reserved. ======================
#
# Compile-equivalence corpus: legacy VBSP/VVIS/VRAD lumps and PVS
# (RFC 0007 R48 "byte-identical legacy lumps and PVS vs legacy executables";
# RFC 0005 Q0 gap corpus, item 2).
#
# Four small authored maps (quality/fixtures/corpus/compile/maps, generated by
# make_maps.py next to them) are compiled vbsp -> vvis -> vrad -ldr ->
# vrad -hdr by the declared executables. Every one of the 64 lumps of the
# result is compared byte for byte with quality/fixtures/corpus/compile/
# expected.json, which the legacy executables recorded. The oracle is this
# file's own stdlib reader of the v21 header, the visibility lump (decoded to
# per-cluster PVS rows), the node tree (point -> cluster, for authored
# visibility expectations) and ColorRGBExp32 lighting; it shares no code with
# the tools.
#
# Determinism policy (the evidence is in expected.json "findings"):
#   * every tool runs with -threads 1, relative argv from the map directory, a
#     fixed environment, and under `setarch x86_64 -R` (ASLR off). Legacy VRAD
#     reads uninitialized stack memory in BuildSupersampleFaceLights (valgrind:
#     "conditional jump depends on uninitialised value ... stack allocation"),
#     so with ASLR or more than one worker its supersampling decisions, and
#     LIGHTING/LIGHTING_HDR/leaf-ambient bytes, vary run to run. With
#     supersampling off (-noextra) the output is identical across ASLR and
#     1/4/32 threads. The policy fixes the execution rather than hiding bytes.
#   * DISPINFO (lump 26) carries bytes VBSP never writes: CDispSubNeighbor
#     fields after an invalid (0xFFFF) neighbor index, CDispCornerNeighbors
#     slots at or beyond m_nNeighbors, and struct padding. Those, and only
#     those, bytes are masked; the rest of the lump is compared exactly.
#   * the suite compiles every map twice and first requires the two results to
#     agree (a nondeterministic host fails `<map>.deterministic`, not the gate).
#
# Modes:
#   compile_equivalence.py [--tools DIR] [--maps a,b] [--seed-fault F]
#       The suite. Seeded faults (negative rows): `lump-byte` flips one
#       LIGHTING byte of box_light; `vis-bit` toggles one PVS bit of
#       three_rooms (re-encoded, so the decoded-PVS comparison names it first);
#       `vrad-noextra` runs VRAD without supersampling, a tool-behaviour change
#       that must surface as a LIGHTING divergence.
#   compile_equivalence.py record --tools DIR [--reference-tools DIR ...]
#       [--study-runs N] [--gdb-probe]
#       Rewrites expected.json and fixture.json from DIR's executables, runs
#       the determinism study, and compares each reference build (for example
#       the pre-fix `ad7120f3^` build) with DIR under the policy, with
#       supersampling off, and as ASLR outcome sets.
#
# Python 3 standard library only.
#
# ============================================================================

